@DATABASE Penwright.guide
@$VER: Penwright.guide 1.0 (08.11.2026)
@AUTHOR Boing BASIC
@WORDWRAP
@NODE Main "Penwright"

@{b}Penwright@{ub} - a word processor for AmigaOS 4

Penwright is written in Boing BASIC. It keeps your text in paragraphs with styles
(headings, quotes, lists, code) and alignment, and every letter can be bold, italic,
underlined, struck through, coloured and sized. It checks your spelling as you type,
finds and replaces, counts words, and saves its own format or exports RTF, HTML and
plain text.

  @{" Writing          " LINK Writing}    typing, moving, selecting
  @{" Styles           " LINK Styles}    character and paragraph styles
  @{" Find and replace " LINK Find}
  @{" Spelling         " LINK Spelling}    the dictionary, learning words
  @{" Files            " LINK Files}    .pwd, RTF, HTML, text; autosave
  @{" Menus and keys   " LINK Keys}
  @{" ARexx            " LINK ARexx}    the PENWRIGHT port and its commands
  @{" Command line     " LINK CLI}
@ENDNODE

@NODE Writing "Writing"
@{b}Writing@{ub}

Type as usual: Return starts a new paragraph, Backspace and Del delete (with Alt or
Ctrl a whole word), Tab inserts four spaces. Click to put the cursor somewhere,
drag to select, double-click to select a word, Shift+click to extend the selection.

Cursor keys move by letters and lines; Alt+Left/Right (or Ctrl) by words;
Alt+Up/Down to the start or end of the document; Shift+Ctrl+Up/Down by a page;
Home/End to the start and end of the line. Hold Shift to select while moving.
The mouse wheel scrolls.

Undo (Amiga-Z) takes back your changes one by one (a run of typing counts as one);
Redo (Amiga-Y) puts them back.

Cut (Amiga-X), Copy (Amiga-C) and Paste (Amiga-V) keep the styles inside Penwright;
the plain text also goes on the system clipboard, and text copied in other programs
pastes in.

The status line shows where the cursor is and the style there.
@ENDNODE

@NODE Styles "Styles"
@{b}Styles@{ub}

@{b}Characters@{ub}: Bold (Amiga-B), Italic (Amiga-I), Underline (Amiga-U), Strike through,
Plain (Amiga-P), a colour (the colour chooser) and a size in points (the size chooser,
or Amiga-> and Amiga-<). With a selection they change the selected text; without one
they change what you type next.

@{b}Paragraphs@{ub}: the style chooser or Amiga-0 .. Amiga-6:
  Body      ordinary text                       Amiga-0
  Heading 1, 2, 3  larger, bold                 Amiga-1 .. 3
  Quote     indented, with a bar                Amiga-4
  Bullet    a list item                         Amiga-5
  Code      not wrapped, on a grey background   Amiga-6
A new paragraph after a heading is body text.

@{b}Alignment@{ub}: left (Amiga-[), centre (Amiga-|), right (Amiga-]) and justified (Amiga-J),
or the alignment chooser.

Note: the canvas font on this system has one size; sizes are kept, saved and
exported, and shown at their size where the screen font supports it.
@ENDNODE

@NODE Find "Find and replace"
@{b}Find and replace@{ub}

Edit > Find (Amiga-F) asks for the text and selects the next match after the
cursor, wrapping round at the end. End the text with " CASE" to match upper and
lower case exactly, with " WORD" to find whole words only (both may be given).
Find next (Amiga-G) repeats the search.

Edit > Replace all (Amiga-R) replaces every match in the document, with the same
CASE and WORD options; the replaced text keeps the style of the text it replaces.
One Undo takes the whole replacement back.
@ENDNODE

@NODE Spelling "Spelling"
@{b}Spelling@{ub}

Words that are not in the dictionary get a red wavy underline (Tools > Mark
misspelt words switches this off). Tools > Check spelling (Amiga-K) selects the next
one and offers suggestions: type the correction, + to add the word to your own
list, or leave it as it is to skip.

The dictionary (penwright.dict, beside the program) holds about 225 000 words from
Webster's Second International (public domain) plus modern words; endings such as
-s, -ed, -ing, -er, -ly and -'s are understood. Your own words are kept in
penwright.words, one per line. Code paragraphs, numbers and short words in capitals
(RTF, HTML) are not checked.
@ENDNODE

@NODE Files "Files"
@{b}Files@{ub}

Penwright documents (.pwd) are plain text: one line per paragraph with its style,
alignment, text and the character styles as runs.

Open reads .pwd, RTF (styles, sizes, colours and alignment; pictures and tables are
skipped) and plain text. Project > Export writes RTF (for other word processors),
HTML (headings, lists, quotes, colours and sizes as CSS) or plain text.
Project > Document info sets the title and author, which go into the RTF and HTML too.

Every two minutes a changed document that has a file name is also saved as
name.pwd.autosave.
@ENDNODE

@NODE Keys "Menus and keys"
@{b}Menus and keys@{ub}

Project    New A-N, Open A-O, Save A-S, Save as, Export RTF / HTML / text,
           Document info, Help, About, Quit A-Q
Edit       Undo A-Z, Redo A-Y, Cut A-X, Copy A-C, Paste A-V, Select all A-A,
           Find A-F, Find next A-G, Replace all A-R
Text       Bold A-B, Italic A-I, Underline A-U, Strike through, Plain A-P, Bigger A->, Smaller A-<
Paragraph  Body A-0, Heading 1-3 A-1..3, Quote A-4, Bullet A-5, Code A-6,
           Align left A-[, Centre A-|, Align right A-], Justify A-J
Tools      Check spelling A-K, Mark misspelt words, Word count A-W, Show paragraph marks A-M

The right mouse button over the page opens a menu with Cut, Copy, Paste, Bold,
Italic and Check spelling.
@ENDNODE

@NODE ARexx "ARexx"
@{b}ARexx@{ub}

Penwright opens the ARexx port PENWRIGHT. Commands (also usable in scripts):

  INSERTTEXT text (\n = new paragraph)   TYPE text   NEWPARAGRAPH   DELETE
  GETTEXT (the selection, or all)   GETPARA n   PARACOUNT   GETCURSOR
  SETCURSOR para offset   SELECT p1 o1 p2 o2   SELECTALL   GETSELECTION
  BOLD|ITALIC|UNDERLINE|STRIKE [ON|OFF]   PLAIN   COLOR 0..15   SIZE points
  STYLE BODY|HEADING1|HEADING2|HEADING3|QUOTE|BULLET|CODE   ALIGN LEFT|CENTER|RIGHT|JUSTIFY
  FIND text [CASE] [WORD]   REPLACEALL "find" "with" [CASE] [WORD]
  WORDCOUNT   CHARCOUNT   UNDO   REDO   COPY   CUT   PASTE
  NEW   OPEN file   SAVE [file]   EXPORT RTF|HTML|TXT file   TITLE text   AUTHOR text
  SPELLNEXT   SUGGEST word   LEARN word   LIVESPELL [OFF]
  MODIFIED   FILENAME   VERSION   QUIT

Example:
  /* letter.rexx */
  ADDRESS PENWRIGHT
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'NEW'
  'INSERTTEXT Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nThank you for your letter.'
  'SELECTALL'
  'SIZE 14'
  'WORDCOUNT'
  SAY RESULT 'words'
@ENDNODE

@NODE CLI "Command line"
@{b}Command line@{ub}

  Penwright [file] [--script commands.pws] [--log results.log]

--script runs the commands of a text file (one per line, as for @{"ARexx" LINK ARexx})
once the window is open and writes each command and its result to the log.
PAUSE n [tag] waits n seconds; QUIT ends the program.
@ENDNODE
